::Q1::What is Amazon Web Services (AWS)?
{
~A single database engine installed on a local computer
~A version control system for storing source code
=A cloud platform providing a broad set of computing services
~A programming language for building cloud applications
} 


::Q2::Which AWS service category is primarily associated with storing files and objects?
{
~Identity and access management
~Developer tools
~Compute
=Storage
}

::Q3::What is a key characteristic of cloud computing pricing described in the module? 
{
~Every AWS service has one fixed lifetime price
~Pricing is unrelated to resource usage
~Customers must purchase all hardware before using a service
=Customers generally pay for the resources and services they use
}

::Q4::What does the shared responsibility model primarily clarify?
{
~Which operating system every AWS service runs
=Which security responsibilities belong to AWS and which belong to the customer
~Which programming language must be used with AWS
~Which database schema customers must use
}

::Q5::What is the customer's responsibility under the shared responsibility model? 
{
~Maintaining AWS's global network hardware
~Manufacturing AWS servers
~All physical security of AWS data centers
=Security tasks that depend on how the customer configures and uses AWS services
}